 "code_head": "dcb43345a3b6755d58725469aa96b9d339427d6d",
 "code_head_note": "Measured at `e9a572d4b499d52050ee29bd2a8bf6cb0ab67134`, which the #12304 rebases rewrote OUT of every ref (it is a dangling local object, absent from a fresh clone), so the field names the latest rebased stand-in instead. EQUIVALENCE IS SCOPED, not global: `git diff e9a572d4b4 ae63e846e410 -- tortoise/entity_resolver.py tortoise/entity_blocking.py tortoise/extractor_v2.py` is EMPTY \u2014 those three files are the code this measurement exercises, and on them the two commits are identical (`git patch-id` agrees). The commit is NOT globally identical to the pre-rebase one \u2014 the whole tree diff is 89 files (`git diff --shortstat e9a572d4b4 ae63e846e410` -> `89 files changed, 25197 insertions(+), 794 deletions(-)`), which is just the base moving under it. ⛔ THE FIELD NAMES A LATER TWIN THAN THIS PARAGRAPH DERIVES — the `#12304` rebase onto `87c07462a8` rewrote the branch once more, so `code_head` is `dcb43345a3b6755d58725469aa96b9d339427d6d`, the rebased twin of `ae63e846e410` in the current generation, and `git diff --quiet ae63e846e410 dcb43345a3b6 -- tortoise/entity_resolver.py tortoise/entity_blocking.py tortoise/extractor_v2.py` is EMPTY, so the equivalence derived above carries through transitively. `code_head` is therefore the ONE sha in this note that resolves today: it is an ancestor of this PR's HEAD and of nothing on `main`, and the rail's squash merge will leave it served by no ref either. The shas that name SUPERSEDED generations — including the measured `e9a572d4b4` — are unreachable from every ref the remote still serves: history, not pointers (see the object-DB paragraph below). The durable identification is the CONTENT anchor, which survives any rebase. Changes to those three files AFTER ae63e846e410: two commits moved only DOCSTRINGS — one moved the `emitted:` note (no statement, no call) and one added the `complete=True` note; neither is named by sha here, because both are pre-rebase objects a reader cannot resolve (the same reason the two label changes below are named by their rebased shas first); `e7f9d77ed5b7` (pre-rebase `d52a989eafd2`) renamed the `lsh_bands` docstring label and the `stats()` counter key `keys`->`key_memberships` \u2014 a LABEL change to a diagnostic dict, with the counter's value and every attach decision unchanged. `fe9cbee4e447` (pre-rebase `22ec4d1a6048`) then added a `candidates(label=None)` LABEL FALLBACK \u2014 the LAST statement change in these three files, i.e. the only one AFTER `e7f9d77ed5b7` \u2014 and this run never reaches it: the harness calls `index.candidates(surface, label=\"Object\")` (the variant arm of `run()`, in `tools/candidate_recall_11901.py`), so the `label is None` branch is not taken. Renamed from `keys` in `index_stats` in `e7f9d77ed5b7` (pre-rebase `d52a989eafd2`): the counter increments once per (member, block) pair, so 10968 is key MEMBERSHIPS across 1000 members, not 10968 distinct keys (the index has 8449 blocks). \u26d4 The list is a SNAPSHOT at this artifact's head, and a docstring-only commit landed after it is NOT named above (the round-7 residual declaration in `entity_blocking.py`'s invariant 3 is one) \u2014 that does not weaken the claim. \u26d4 The claim about commits AFTER `ae63e846e410` is NOT what the `git diff` above proves: that compares two fixed commits and says nothing about anything later. It is re-proved by ENUMERATING them and comparing docstring-stripped ASTs per commit \u2014 `git log --format=%h ae63e846e410..HEAD -- tortoise/entity_resolver.py tortoise/entity_blocking.py tortoise/extractor_v2.py` -> the commits listed by that command. ⛔ THAT RANGE NO LONGER ISOLATES POST-RUN CHANGES: the #12304 rebases rewrote every branch sha, so `ae63e846e410..HEAD` now spans the whole rewritten branch — no count is stated here: an integer quoting a range this same PR keeps extending is a number a reader cannot re-derive, and a count a reader cannot re-derive is the defect this note exists to stop and `d52a989eafd2` / `22ec4d1a6048` were rewritten out of every ref that reaches HEAD along with it — and ⛔ NOT out of the object DB: both survive as OBJECTS in THIS checkout only — no ref the remote serves reaches them: the `#12304` force-pushes moved the local `refs/remotes/origin/fix/12295-fold-blocking` onto a later generation, so `git merge-base --is-ancestor` now answers 1 against it, and the tip of the generation that DID contain them (`ff0a7be3ec`) is itself unreachable. An object DB is not a reference a reader can follow, so those shas are named as history, never as pointers. So naming them is not a reference a reader can follow — naming them is a dead sha a reader cannot resolve. The two STATEMENT changes this note names are therefore identified by their CONTENT, and their shas in the rebased generation are `e7f9d77ed5b7` (`git log -S'key_memberships'`: the `stats()` counter key `keys` -> `key_memberships`, a diagnostic LABEL — which is why this artifact's field reads `key_memberships` while the run that produced it emitted `keys`) and `fe9cbee4e447` (`git log -S'every label this index actually holds'`: the `candidates(label=None)` fallback, which this run never reaches). Both are members of that enumerated list. The rest of the list is NOT claimed to be docstring-only: it is a base-moved range, so it holds the branch's own feature and fix commits as well. \u26d4 THE SCOPE ABOVE IS THE PRODUCT CODE, AND IT IS NOT THE WHOLE STORY \u2014 the code that PRODUCES this artifact is the harness `tools/candidate_recall_11901.py`, and it moved between the run and `code_head`: `git diff --stat e9a572d4b4 ae63e846e410 -- tools/candidate_recall_11901.py` is `494 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)` \u2014 the #12294 name-entropy arms came in with the base move. So a re-run AT `code_head` emits SIX arms this artifact does not contain: `gate`, `gate_by_class`, `gate_gated_names`, `gate_variant`, `pooled_coverage`, `pooled_gate`, every one an unconditional `arms[...] = ...` assignment in today's harness (16 assigned there vs the 10 held here: blocking / duplicate_rate / exact* / pooled / variant*). \u26d4 ENUMERATE that set, never grep for a couple of names \u2014 `grep -c 'gate_variant\\|pooled_gate'` reads 0 at `git show e9a572d4b4:tools/candidate_recall_11901.py` and 7 at `ae63e846e410`, which is how an earlier cut of this note undercounted the set by four and then asserted \"no gate arms\" beside a harness that assigns `arms[\"gate\"]`. The check is `git show <code_head>:tools/candidate_recall_11901.py | grep -o 'arms\\[\"[a-z_]*\"\\]' | sort -u` against this artifact's own `arms` keys. \u26d4 READ THIS AS THE REPRODUCTION CONTRACT: these numbers are the RUN's, produced by the harness as it stood at `e9a572d4b4`; re-running at `code_head` reproduces the ARMS this artifact holds (blocking, duplicate_rate, exact*, pooled, variant*) but emits those six EXTRA arms whose absence here is the base having moved, not a lost measurement. Re-running the #12294 arms is a separate run and is committed separately (`measurement-entropy-gate-12294.json`).",
